                  "id": "Kxfw1",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 900,
                  "content": "A label and its input are one object; two fields are two. Label→input is 8pt, field→field is 12pt, section gaps are 20 or 28pt. The ratio between the first two gaps is the rule, not either number. Every assistive line — hint, echo or error — occupies the same reserved row, so turning an error on never moves the fields below it. Assistive copy under 15pt uses Secondary, never Muted. Over media the same field moves to the Inputs glass tier and its type flips to white.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
