                  "fill": "$ink",
                  "content": "Navigation and chrome",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 28,
                  "fontWeight": "600",
                  "letterSpacing": -0.5
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Ot0ba",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 900,
                  "content": "Glass is a functional material, not a decorative card style, and it only works over something worth seeing through to. Sheet 1 defines four tiers; chrome uses two of them. The floating bottom bar sits on Tab Bar at 38%, and sheets and menus sit on Share + Filters at 75%, which is near-opaque enough to take dark type. Never place glass over a flat fill, never stack glass on glass — the travelling selection capsule is the single exception, because it is navigation chrome inside navigation chrome. Validate the bar over light, dark, tinted and high-contrast content, at larger text sizes, and with Reduce Transparency on.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "rectangle",
                  "id": "vU8An",
