                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "m1AMh1",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 820,
                  "content": "The assistant's connector is a small file the user opens once, and it runs on their machine. Its tool surface is generated from the share, not written into the file — so most of what looks like a new feature is a new share, and needs no re-install. Only genuinely new local code does. The interface owns that distinction, because it is the one thing a user will get wrong.",
